/-!
# Actual integral specialization kernels in degrees one, two, and three

The three degrees use one genuine four-torus source homeomorphism, with
the original period order `(β₀, β₁, α₀, α₁)`.  Geometric surjectivity and
the actual monodromy homotopy identify the kernels with the integral
images of the corresponding monodromy differences.  The degree-two and
degree-three formulas use the original exterior-power markings.

The quotient equivalences have the actual specialization map as their
forward map on representatives.  Small-drift and radius-less-than-one
conditions are derived from holomorphicity, not assumed at the original
ambient radius.
-/
